","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMjI3NDc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuennancy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuennancy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuennancy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuennancy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuennancy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuennancy","user_view_type":"public"},"commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2024-02-28T20:54:42Z","event":"labeled","id":11957438076,"intent":null,"label":{"color":"d73a4a","name":"bug 🐞"},"node_id":"LE_lADODGgK6M6AvLsIzwAAAALIuAZ8","performed_via_github_app":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/events/11957438076"},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bjacob","id":79535,"login":"bjacob","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NTM1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"@benvanik, The first report about this line, https://github.com/openxla/iree/blob/76cbaaca2cf44ac0e4f58cbce4134c253e38f758/runtime/src/iree/io/memory_stream.c#L267\r\n\r\nAnd the code path for loading an unaligned uint16 goes here:\r\nhttps://github.com/openxla/iree/blob/76cbaaca2cf44ac0e4f58cbce4134c253e38f758/runtime/src/iree/base/alignment.h#L364-L366\r\n\r\nIt is always undefined behavior to have a C or C++ object at a memory location whose address isn't a multiple of its alignment, so the UBSan report seems to be correct. No platform-specific trait can change that. Instead, platform-specific traits such as `__ARM_FEATURE_UNALIGNED` only merely mean an existence claim, that there is *some* way to perform an unaligned access. They don't suddenly change the C/C++ semantics to allow unaligned objects. In the case of `__ARM_FEATURE_UNALIGNED`, the Arm reference https://developer.arm.com/documentation/dui0774/g/chr1383660321827 explains __ARM_FEATURE_UNALIGNED as \"Set to 1 if the target supports unaligned access in hardware\".  This could mean a number of things (I don't know exactly in this case), such as possibly meaning that some builtin or intrinsic is available to perform that, I dont know --- but `alignment.h` in its current form is undefined behavior and the easy way out for now would be to just build with `IREE_MEMORY_ACCESS_ALIGNMENT_REQUIRED_*`.","created_at":"2024-02-28T21:07:49Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/16608#issuecomment-1969918686","id":1969918686,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/16608","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M51apLe","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1969918686/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-28T21:08:08Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1969918686","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/followers","following_url":"http