pos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Unrelated to whether we should act on the errors: Is it expected behavior that these errors don't fail the tests? ","created_at":"2024-02-28T22:31:39Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/16608#issuecomment-1970030930","id":1970030930,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/16608","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M51bElS","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1970030930/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-28T22:31:39Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1970030930","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/309732?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/julianwa","id":309732,"login":"julianwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwOTczMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bjacob","id":79535,"login":"bjacob","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NTM1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"yes, typical. this undefined behavior could translate into anything in theory, but when the target load/store instructions don't have any alignment requirement, that would \"just work\". When the target load/store instructions do have an alignment requirement, the observed behavior would be a crash. On some target architectures, both kinds of instructions exist so it can be a matter of luck that determines in which cases you fall. And when the compiler can tell at compile time that the address is going to be misaligned, some wilder things can happen, such as, simply omitting the load/store on the basis that \"it would be undefined behavior anyway if it happened\".","created_at":"2024-02-29T02:56:54Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/16608#issuecomment-1970307499","id":1970307499,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/16608","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M51cIGr","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1970307499/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-29T02:56:54Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1970307499","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bjacob","id":79535,"login":"bjacob","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NTM1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob","user_view_type":"public"}}]}
